{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1548465-for-want-of-a-better-magic-system-adapting-mage-the-awakening-magic-for-d-d-5e","id":1548465,"title":"For Want of a Better Magic System - Adapting Mage: The Awakening magic for D&D 5e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-13T03:09:41-08:00","id":1548465,"title":"For Want of a Better Magic System - Adapting Mage: The Awakening magic for D&D 5e?","content":"I have a group of long-time gaming friends who have played a great variety of systems. For the last several years we've been deep in D&amp;D 5e, for better or for worse.<br /> <br /> Everyone admits that the Vancian magic system in D&amp;D is clunky and unimaginative, and some of us have wondered about how it might be possible to translate Mage's super-flexible-yet-coherent system over and graft it successfully. Those delightful features like improvised magic, sympathetic magic, the elegant layout of the Arcana, and so on.<br /> <br /> I'm very concept-minded but not so strong in terms of numbers, while my friends tend to be very crunch-oriented and want to see math that makes sense and maintains some semblance of balance.<br /> <br /> Anyone ever try this? Has it worked at all? If not, how can it be made to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28554-jean-renaud","name":"Jean-Renaud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28554_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T02:27:26-08:00","id":1548511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jean-Renaud</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1548465-for-want-of-a-better-magic-system-adapting-mage-the-awakening-magic-for-d-d-5e#post1548465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone ever try this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. I've personally tried to port it to other systems (usually <i>BRP</i>, but there was one attempt at <i>Cthulhu Dark</i>), and it almost always became more hassle than it was worth very quickly.<br /> <br /> I've also read <i>Magus Hack</i> which is essentially Mage: The Ascension but in a sort of OSR style (I think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T06:42:08-08:00","id":1548515,"title":"","content":"I'm also not aware of any existing attempts, but I have now given some thought about how to do this.<br /> It would be a herculean task. D&amp;D and MtA's magic systems are inherently mathematically incompatible. Not only are the dice and resolution systems completely different, there's just no way you can map the five Arcana ratings to the nine spell levels of D&amp;D. There's also the problem of different classes in D&amp;D having different ways of learning and memorizing spells which is somewhat key to distinguishing them, which simply won't work with improvised magic at all (regardless if you port it from MtA or use something else) without some sort of rework.<br /> All of that means you cannot simply port most of the MtA concepts without also significantly reworking and rewriting them. (The one exception I can think of is adding up-casting options based on what you can spend Reach on to model the extra Reach given to mages with Arcana ratings above the spell's dot rating.) You'd also have to significantly rework about every magic-related class and subclass feature (which, for the full caster classes, is almost all of them) to work with the new system. And, of course, manage to do all of that while still being balanced level-by-level to D&amp;D's math.<br /> <br /> That is not to say I don't think it's possible. I think it absolutely is, given enough enthusiasm and effort (especially if your group isn't hugely concerned with balance, but that's not how you seem to describe your players).<br /> But if the goal is primarily to improve D&amp;D's magic system for your group, I would absolutely recommend looking up other homebrew improvised systems designed specifically to replace D&amp;D's vancian system rather than transplant MtA's magic system. Sorry to be a downer, but I think that's much easier and much more viable than trying to transplant a system between two very different games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T06:09:44-08:00","id":1548762,"title":"","content":"The first question - how far do you actually want to go?<br /> <br /> D&amp;D is foundationally game of resource management, and advancement is quantitative - earn XP, get more hitpoints, bigger sword. For all their differences Burning Hands and Prismatic Spray are substantively similar. Vancian magic may be &quot;clunky and unimaginative&quot;, but it continues to work for D&amp;D because it fits the resource management paradigm.<br /> <br /> If your friends are crunch-and-balance focused, then I'm presuming (and tell me if I'm wrong) they play D&amp;D &quot;the way God intended&quot;; narrative framing stringing together the skill checks and combat encounters. In which case you're not going to fundamentally change the paradigm - otherwise you and your friends will be sat at the same table, playing different games.<br /> <br /> The first thing that comes to my mind is something like:<ul><li>Skill checks to cast (like Truenamers) rather than Spells-per-day, replacing finite uses with unreliability of each use (like Fighters do)</li> <li>Spells (Rotes) are largely as normal so that we have predictable rule-bundles. but rather than the 1-9 spell levels they have an Arcanum Level rated 1-5.</li> <li>5 subclasses (Watchtowers) that determine how your Arcana level up - Ruling Arcana go up when a wizard would get access to odd-level spells, Common Arcana on the even spell levels, and Inferior Arcana go up with Common but at -1.</li> <li>You can roll a skill check of some kind to cast any spell you meet the Arcana requisite for.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T14:40:07-08:00","id":1548770,"title":"","content":"I do appreciate all of the responses so far. A lot of food for thought!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28554-jean-renaud","name":"Jean-Renaud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28554_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T19:35:35-08:00","id":1548776,"title":"","content":"TBH, if I wanted to play a Mage-like character today, I wouldn't want to go to the trouble of building a whole new class, since I only need enough rules for one character.<br /> <br /> I think my first probably try to talk my DM into letting me re-theme an Expanded Psionics Handbook psionic class, with a custom power list based on a Watchtower. Psionics are nice because they're point- rather than slot-based, but mostly because their powers tend toward some improv - compare, say, Astral Construct to Summon Monster or Energy Burst to Fireball.<br /> <br /> I think you could do a strong approximation of Prime, Forces, Time, Mind, and Space right out of the box - Obrimos-alikes and Mastigos-alikes should be easy. I think there's reasonable representation of other Arcana, and if not there definitely isn't anything you couldn't patch with some judiciously borrowed Wizard or Cleric spells if you needed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T00:45:15-08:00","id":1548779,"title":"","content":"Notice that it's possible to stretch 5 Arcana ratings towards 9 Spell levels, if you take Reach allocation into account - just like Legacy Attainments do. For example: <i>Rewrite History</i> is a 4 dot spell, but it could require anywhere between 0 and 8 Reach, placing it in different Spell levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T04:20:33-08:00","id":1548782,"title":"","content":"However, in a system with improvisation, you end up getting longer gaps before you unlock new effects.<br /> D&amp;D RAW gets you access to new spells every second character level (ignoring the last four levels). Doing the same with just five levels of an Arcanum would mean getting access to new spell effects every fourth character level, which is quite the drought where you merely get better with the spell effects you already have access to for long periods of time, which definitely risks becoming boring to play.<br /> Sure, you could divide the Practices more granularly to fill out more spell levels, but that leads to weird behaviour where you learn complementary effects out of sync (Patterning/Unravelling, Making/Unmaking) and/or get character levels where you always learn quite specific types of effects, like information gathering (Knowing and/or Unveiling) or defensive effects (Shielding), which would feel weird and awkward to me.<br /> <br /> A workaround that could work is to level two different Arcana. You still stay quite a long time at each Arcanum rating for the individual Arcana, but at least you gain new spell effects (even if they're the same Practices you already had access to, you can apply them in whole bew ways).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T10:54:19-08:00","id":1548793,"title":"","content":"Tying Practices to spell level advancement the same way the tie to Arcana is already tricky, and might not be possible depending on how you want to play.<br /> <br /> If at 1st level I can only access knowing/compelling/unveiling, is that character going to be fun to play? Maybe if, like a Bard, I have some other way to contribute to combat encounters... but I'd have a hard time feeling like a &quot;primary caster&quot;?<br /> <br /> This may be mostly a &quot;level 1 problem&quot; but my point is something about Mage's arcanum ratings probably has to change at least a little, just to fit the &quot;higher strength/bigger rock&quot; advancement paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T15:29:36-08:00","id":1548798,"title":"","content":"I admit I haven't given this much thought, but I'd consider looking at Monte Cooke's World of Darkness. While more inspired by Ascension than Awakening, it was a fairly valiant attempt to make freeform mages work in a d20 system (along with many of the other cWoD critters, though it's really it's own setting).<br /> <br /> It might not be everything you're looking for, but it might be a way to cut back a lot of the work by getting some of the basic ground work already done for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}